From: T43b worker <local>
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] droidloom-wayland: enable host text input without host keyboard focus (T38 #65, OSK deadlock)

The host's on-screen keyboard (phosh-osk-stub) is a layer surface.  While it
is mapped it holds the compositor's keyboard focus, so the Android client that
is waiting for text input is *not* the focused task.  Requiring
`Some(editor.task) == focused_task` therefore deadlocks as soon as the OSK has
ever been shown: no `zwp_text_input_v3.enable` is sent, so the OSK never
returns, so the client never regains keyboard focus.

`entered` already ties the request to this client's own text-input surface
(`zwp_text_input_v3.enter` ⇒ `task_for_surface()`), so accept the editor when
the compositor reports no focused Android task at all.

Measured on TB322FC (phoc 0.46 + edge-swipe, droidloom release 51):
- before: probe `focused_task=None` ⇒ `desired=None` ⇒ no enable ⇒ 小红书
  phone field / Android Settings search show no host keyboard;
- after: same state, `desired=Some(..)` ⇒ enable ⇒ numeric OSK appears on a
  single finger tap, typing 10 digits keeps the OSK up.

---
--- a/graphics/droidloom-wayland/src/text_input.rs
+++ b/graphics/droidloom-wayland/src/text_input.rs
@@ -242,10 +242,16 @@
     }
 
     pub fn update(&mut self, focused_task: Option<u64>) {
+        // The host's on-screen keyboard is a layer surface that holds the
+        // compositor's keyboard focus while it is mapped, so the app waiting
+        // for text input is *not* the focused task. Requiring `focused_task`
+        // here deadlocks once the OSK has ever been mapped: no enable ⇒ no
+        // OSK ⇒ the app never regains keyboard focus. `entered` already ties
+        // the request to this client's own text-input surface.
         let desired = self.editor.filter(|editor| {
             editor.active
                 && editor.task != 0
-                && Some(editor.task) == focused_task
+                && focused_task.is_none_or(|task| task == editor.task)
                 && self.entered.is_some()
         });
         // T38 (#65), break ① of the causal chain: Android's `showSoftInput`
